    "evidence_text": "Radford et al.\n\n4.\n\nBy concatenating these values, a vector is generated which is given as input to a fully connected network.\n\nWe also include the details of our implementation and error analysis in the respective subsections.\n\nExperiments and Results ::: Dataset Description\tWe evaluate our method on two\n\nwidely-studied datasets provided by Waseem and Hovey  and Davidson et al. .\n\nThey annotated their dataset manually as racism, sexism, or neither.\n\nIn detail, the distribution of different classes in both datasets will be provided\n\nWe also convert all tweets to lower case.\n\nBased on our experiments, we trained our classifier with a batch size of\n\n32 for 3 epochs.\n\nThe dropout probability is set to 0.1 for all layers.\n\nAdam optimizer is used with a learning rate of 2e-5.\n\nAs an input, we tokenized each tweet with the BERT tokenizer.\n\nClasses' distribution of train, validation, and test datasets are shown\n\nin Table TABREF16.\n\nbaselines.\n\ndepicted in Figures FIGREF19 and FIGREF19.\n\nBERT\u2019s layers and a set of features associated to the different type of biases in data.",
